        "id": 1314845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-20T18:58:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e The current panic data structure is not adjusted to store that info.\n\nIt looks like the maybe the information is [copied](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/zephyr/shim/src/panic.c;l\u003d210-213;drc\u003d3e98a43be6e8b2319f28a6ded36135116f960c5c) in [this case](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/zephyr/shim/src/panic.c;l\u003d161-169;drc\u003d3e98a43be6e8b2319f28a6ded36135116f960c5c). Shouldn\u0027t that same logic apply in the [`if` case](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/zephyr/shim/src/panic.c;l\u003d156-160;drc\u003d3e98a43be6e8b2319f28a6ded36135116f960c5c)? (It looks like you can\u0027t call `panic_set_reason` directly since it will overwrite the other data that is copied, but you could pull [this logic](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/zephyr/shim/src/panic.c;l\u003d210-213;drc\u003d3e98a43be6e8b2319f28a6ded36135116f960c5c) into a separate function. If this makes sense and you want to change `shim/src/panic.c`, you could check that the [`panic_data` test](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/test/panic_data.c) passes after making the change.",
      "parentUuid": "f04bc7a6_4ac086e8",
      "revId": "614229c93845d214709275fb0e79017834f12a58",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
