      "writtenOn": "2024-05-21T05:39:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for the suggestion. Actually, I added the [logic](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/zephyr/shim/src/panic.c;l\u003d161-169;drc\u003d3e98a43be6e8b2319f28a6ded36135116f960c5c) to store the reason. I\u0027ve been thinking about storing it in every case. The problem is the architecture of panic data structure. For ARM, the panic [exception/info/reason](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/zephyr/shim/src/panic.c;l\u003d65-67;drc\u003d3e98a43be6e8b2319f28a6ded36135116f960c5c) are stored in place of [regs IPSR/R4/R5](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/include/panic_defs.h;l\u003d46-49). While IPSR is a duplication of xPSR, so it is not a problem, we would overwrite values of R4/R5 regs provided with the esf structure.",
      "parentUuid": "52ae8d45_199921c1",
      "revId": "614229c93845d214709275fb0e79017834f12a58",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
